# oracle: pair brownian (colloid package doc example pair_style brownian 1.5 1 1 2.01 2.5 2.0 5878567, pair_coeff * *) on about 170 monodisperse spheres (radius 1, the doc example assumes radius 1) on a simple cubic lattice (spacing 2.15) in a 12 x 12 x 12 periodic box, 30 steps with fix nve/sphere: the log terms (flaglog 1) with the FLD isotropic terms (flagfld 1), flagHI and flagVF on
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.9e-15, atoms 6.1e-15.
# native: installed lmp (b332f28)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      sphere
boundary        p p p
region          box block 0 12 0 12 0 12
create_box      1 box
lattice         sc 0.1
create_atoms    1 box
set             type 1 diameter 2.0
set             type 1 density 1.0
pair_style      brownian 1.5 1 1 2.01 2.5 2.0 5878567
pair_coeff      * *
fix             1 all nve/sphere
compute         rot all erotate/sphere
thermo_style    custom step pe ke c_rot
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
timestep        0.0001
thermo          10
run             30
